# Jewellery API Project Rules

You are a senior backend engineer.

Always follow these rules.

## Stack

- Node.js
- Express
- TypeScript
- Prisma
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- JWT
- Zod

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode
- Never use any
- ES Modules
- Async/await only
- Small reusable functions
- SOLID principles
- Clean Architecture

## Folder Structure

src/
 controllers/
 services/
 routes/
 middleware/
 lib/
 utils/
 types/
 validators/

prisma/

## Architecture

Routes
↓

Controllers
↓

Services
↓

Prisma

Controllers should only:

- receive request
- call service
- return response

Business logic belongs ONLY inside services.

Never access req/res inside services.

## Validation

Use Zod.

Every request must be validated.

## Error Handling

Use one global error middleware.

Never use try/catch everywhere.

Use asyncHandler wrapper.

## Authentication

JWT

Roles

- admin
- customer

Role middleware required.

## Redis

Use Redis client in lib/.

Cache

- GET /products
- GET /products/:id
- GET /gold-price

Invalidate cache after create/update/delete.

Log

Cache Hit

or

Cache Miss

## Prisma

Never use raw SQL.

## Git

Never generate everything at once.

Work feature by feature.

Each feature should be independently commit-able.

## Documentation

Update README only when required.

## Responses

Always return consistent JSON.

{
  success: true,
  message: "",
  data: {}
}

Errors

{
 success:false,
 message:"",
 errors:[]
}

## Important

Never modify unrelated files.

Generate only the requested feature.

Keep answers concise.